ocument-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5328256-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5328256</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-61281778-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>61281778</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-6217213-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>6217213</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7294844-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7294844</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8179275-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8179275</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAEDA YOSIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OLYMPUS OPTICAL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIMOTO NAOYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEDA, YOSIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OLYMPUS OPTICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIMOTO, NAOYA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAEDA YOSIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIMOTO NAOYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEDA, YOSIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIMOTO, NAOYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A head-mounted display comprises a lighting circuit (52) for applying a boosted voltage to lighting means (48) for lighting an LCD (47); a video signal detector (42) for detecting the presence of an input video signal; a power controller (49) that produces a supply voltage for the lighting circuit (52) in the presence of a video signal and does not in the absence of a video signal; and a light pulse controller (51) that produces a narrow pulse when the supply voltage from power controller (49) is high and produces a wide pulse when the supply voltage is low. The lighting circuit (52) increases the voltage to a small extent for a short pulse and to a great extent for a long pulse, with the result that a substantally constant voltage is applied to the lighting means (48).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Le visiocasque de la présente invention comprend un circuit d'éclairage (12) permettant d'appliquer à des organes d'éclairage (48) une surtension de façon à éclairer un afficheur à cristaux liquides (47). Un détecteur de signal vidéo (42) surveille la présence d'un signal vidéo d'entrée. Un régulateur de puissance (49) produit une tension d'alimentation pour le circuit d'éclairage (52) en présence d'un signal vidéo. Un contrôleur d'impulsion d'éclairage (51) produit des impulsions courtes pour une tension d'alimentation élevée du régulateur de puissance (49) mais longues pour une tension d'alimentation basse. Le circuit d'éclairage (52) augmente la tension d'une petite quantité en cas d'impulsion courte, et d'une grande quantité en cas d'impulsion longue. Il en résulte l'application d'une tension sensiblement constante aux organes d'éclairage (48).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>